  "taskCall": {
    "context": "# Goal\nTameshi round 35 (verification-fixture craft), WAVE 2 under policy v1 (band 32-64): 58 seats. Lane tip at dispatch `7da6e076c2e25936a3b60dde2a4080d8f05b7e5b`. This is the resume of attempt 2: attempt 1's single v2 wave (64 seats) was dispatched at 18:02 and its L1 session was OOM-killed minutes later; six of its seat reports survived uncommitted and are now inherited evidence under `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-35/w1/` (ExecPristine, RevengerRootShape, ReviewPanelDistinct, ReviewSealedGate, ScribeReport, SealAcceptCommentBlock). Those six items are NOT in this wave; do not write into `w1/`. Everything else here is re-dispatched because its report never landed.\n\nClaims under attack: C1 (depth; `tools/tally-audit-v3.py` kills every kill specimen and accepts every accept specimen on an 8-copy public panel and a sealed set authored after the freeze; the runner stays byte-identical) and C2 (calibration; six self-assessment mismatch classes are zero). C2 already measured PASS at `d16f9b5a` (receipt `.ufo/evidence/round-35/after/c2-at-d16f9b5a.stdout`); it must be re-counted at head after this wave's records land.\n\nPre-data amendments already landed (contract.json A4/A5), routed from wave-1 seats — attack the FIXED apparatus, not the old one:\n- A4: the auto (auto,KEEP) triples now run with the runner's REAL auto root `/tmp/tameshi-r4-2-regression.XXXXXX`; the panel gained two root-keyed kill copies. Wave-1 seat RevengerRootShape's CRITICAL false-accept is the class this closes — try to reopen it.\n- A5: sealed provenance is now anchored to the commit that first added contract.json, requires strict ancestry + lineage creation, and scores bytes committed at REV, not the working tree. Wave-1 seat ReviewSealedGate's BOUNDs are the classes to reopen.\n\n# Frozen artifacts (NEVER edit; read-only)\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/tools/tally-audit-v3.py` sha256 ef98fc5367cdb12c71b8b0ddfb5b83835100831f545f6510437dc84014865885\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/tools/tally-audit-v2.py` sha256 7b11ba25aead93678aef50606b7521fb7c3a85bea47b5ec220a47865b3598d10 (predecessor; the control)\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/tools/mutate-and-run.sh` sha256 a7d3f2dd7d47511a4769aab610dd85d1a37e77b32f14fd763f3af638dd912eb9 (byte-pinned, NEVER edited)\n- `.ufo/evidence/round-35/c1/c1-measure.py` sha256 515b0b1b00b970f31c08e80eb74512ecae0cf1082ddeccfcb373e810cd0559e8 and `.ufo/evidence/round-35/c2/c2-measure.py` sha256 67bb71188cde259088646f960b6fda8e0a217fad5d8260e379054b381018f9cc (frozen counters)\n- `.ufo/evidence/round-35/c1/panel/` (public panel, 5 kill + 3 accept specimens)\n\n# Sealed-authoring items (Seal*) — the rule\nYou author ONE held-out specimen and put the JSON in your REPORT (fenced block); the L1 transcribes it into `.ufo/evidence/round-35/c1/sealed/` and commits it. Ground truth is BEHAVIOR: extract the tally block and run it under all four (auto,KEEP) triples — the auto triples use the runner's real root `/tmp/tameshi-r4-2-regression.XXXXXX`, never a fixed literal — and compare (exit, FULL stdout) of pristine vs copy over at least the all-zero, one-1, one-2, one-3, one-255 and two mixed vectors. A kill specimen must diverge under at least one triple; an accept specimen must be identical on every triple and vector. Do NOT use the tool as your source of truth (it is the object under test); a label your construction does not meet must be reported honestly, not forced.\n\n# Bounds (hard)\n- Your tools start at the FLEET ROOT. Every path you use MUST be absolute; a relative path such as `.ufo/waves/...` lands in the FLEET repo and is a scope violation. Every `Report:` trailer the dispatcher prints is relative to /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin — write it at /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/<that path>, which is the ONLY lane path you may create.\n- NEVER write inside any git checkout's `.git`, never run a mutating jj or git command, never edit the lane, the fleet repo, sibling lanes, `.ufo/state/`, or any file under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/ except your own report. All scratch work goes under /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r35-w2/<YourName>/ (fall back to /tmp if /fast is full).\n- Do not run `pacman` at all (host transactions are paused). Tooling directive (operator 2026-10-19): you may install or upgrade tools that help the task without asking, via `uv tool install`, `npx`, or an official release binary into `~/.local/bin` — official sources only, never piped remote scripts; record tool/version/channel/reason in your report.\n- A finding counts only with the exact command, its exit code, and the bytes/hash it relied on. No fabricated verdicts; a bounded negative (\"class X is closed at this pin, here is the proof\") is a first-class result.\n- Depth limit 3: you are a leaf. Never spawn a swarm; at most one read-only `labrat` probe if your item says so.\n\n# Background you must read first (absolute paths)\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-35/contract.json` (frozen claims, kill rule, amendments A4/A5)\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/waves/round-35/w1/RevengerRootShape.md` and `ReviewSealedGate.md` (the wave-1 findings the amendments answer)\n- `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/corpus/lessons/round-34.md` (the Holds this round attacks)\n- the tool's own docstring (`tools/tally-audit-v3.py:1-100`) for the four round-35 fixes\n",
    "tasks": [
      {
        "name": "SealCfg00Guard",
        "agent": "executor",
        "task": "/skill:godspeed\n\n---\nname: godspeed\ndescription: >\n  Godspeed posture — name the axes, iterate cheap in parallel, keep moves that\n  improve any axis and harm none, and don't aim (let the frontier walk itself).\n  Stops clarifying questions and verbose planning in favor of large concurrent\n  tool-call batches. Use for any task framed with godspeed. Triggers: \"godspeed\",\n  \"--with godspeed\", \"/skill:godspeed\", or a task marked with godspeed framing.\n---\nYou are a Godspeed-enabled subagent.\n\n1. **Name the axes.**\n2. **Iterate cheap, in parallel.**\n3. **Keep moves that improve any axis and harm none.**\n4. **Don't aim — let the frontier walk itself.**\n\n## IMMEDIATELY STOP ASKING CLARIFYING QUESTIONS. Execute tool calls concurrently in large batches. Do not serialize what can run in parallel. Do not output philosophical reasoning or verbose plans. Act directly via tool calls.\n\n# Target\nSetup: `mkdir -p /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r35-seats/SealCfg00Guard && env -u GIT_DIR -u GIT_WORK_TREE -u GIT_INDEX_FILE git clone -q --no-hardlinks /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r35-seats/SealCfg00Guard/lane && env -u GIT_DIR -u GIT_WORK_TREE -u GIT_INDEX_FILE git -C /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r35-seats/SealCfg00Guard/lane checkout -q --detach 7da6e076c2e25936a3b60dde2a4080d8f05b7e5b`. All work happens under /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r35-seats/SealCfg00Guard/ ; the lane checkout is READ-ONLY (never commit, never write inside .../lane). \n\nYou are authoring ONE sealed held-out specimen for the round-35 C1 counter, AFTER its freeze. Work only in /fast/scratch/hyaku/tameshi-r35-seats/SealCfg00Guard/.\nRead the freeze contract and the public panel first: `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-35/contract.json` and `/home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/.ufo/evidence/round-35/c1/panel/`.\nA specimen is a JSON `{\"copies\":[{\"class\":\"<name>\",\"set\":\"kill\"|\"accept\",\"edits\":[[\"<old>\",\"<new>\",<count>]]}]}` whose edits apply to the PINNED runner text (`git -C .../lane show 7da6e076c2e25936a3b60dde2a4080d8f05b7e5b:tools/mutate-and-run.sh`), each old string exactly `count` times.\nGround truth is BEHAVIOR, not opinion: extract the tally block and run it under all four (auto,KEEP) triples — (0,1),(1,0),(0,0),(1,1) with roots of your choosing — and compare (exit, FULL stdout) of pristine vs copy on at least: all-zero, one status 1, one status 2, one status 3, one status 255, and two mixed vectors.\nREQUIRED DELIVERABLE in your report: the JSON content (fenced block), the behavioral receipt table (per config × vector: pristine tuple, copy tuple, equal?), and the sha256 of the copy's resulting runner text. A `kill` specimen must diverge under at least one config; an `accept` specimen must be identical on every config and vector. If your first construction does not meet its label, say so and either fix it (report both) or reject it honestly.\nDo NOT run the tool on your specimen as the source of truth — the tool is what is being tested. You may run it last as an observation, labeled as such.\n\nCLASS TO AUTHOR: a **kill** copy whose divergence appears ONLY under the (auto=0, KEEP=0) triple, gated on a different construct than the public `cfg00-accept-swap` (e.g. gate the SETUP arm, or the sum guard, or a counter reset — not the FAIL arm).\n\n# Acceptance\n- Report at the absolute path named by your `Report:` trailer (under /home/vgpnk/Projects/shokunin/tameshi-shokunin/).\n- Name exact commands, exit codes, sha256s; every claim carries a pointer. Findings are ranked: CRITICAL (a claim is false), BOUND (a real but fail-closed limit), HYGIENE.\n- Your report must state what you attacked, what you found, and what you could NOT break (with the proof).\n\n\nLane bounds: leaf member — no subagent dispatch except your single labrat.\nJudged on: depth\n\nReport: write your scoped findings to .ufo/waves/round-35/w2/SealCfg00Guard.md"
      },
      {
